+F1 — P1 — Live’s server endpoint would gain page-reading accidentally.  
+Evidence: the plan adds `read_web_page` to `toolsFor("guide")` while leaving it out of `GUIDE_TOOLS` ([plan:149](/var/tmp/spideryarn-worktrees/qi-qsy8nqyt-guide-reads-pages/docs/plans/261017e-bring-a-web-page-into-chat.md:149)). Live advertises only `GUIDE_TOOLS` ([live.ts:451](/var/tmp/spideryarn-worktrees/qi-qsy8nqyt-guide-reads-pages/src/live.ts:451)), but its endpoint first accepts every name in `LIVE_SERVER_TOOLS`, which includes `read_web_page`, then calls `runTool` with `kind: "guide"` ([routes.ts:4991](/var/tmp/spideryarn-worktrees/qi-qsy8nqyt-guide-reads-pages/src/routes.ts:4991), [routes.ts:5006](/var/tmp/spideryarn-worktrees/qi-qsy8nqyt-guide-reads-pages/src/routes.ts:5006)). Once `toolsFor("guide")` contains the tool, that second gate permits it. Worse, this endpoint creates a fresh `ToolContext` for each call, so the WeakMap counter would reset and provide no Live cap.  
+Recommended change: add an explicit Live-guide server allowlist based on `GUIDE_TOOLS`, not `toolsFor("guide")`, and test a direct `POST …/live-tool` asking a guide to `read_web_page`, asserting no fetch. Live should remain without this tool.
+
+F2 — P1 — The proposed prompt change omits the shared web-link provenance rules needed for source chips.  
+Evidence: every normal web-capable prompt carries `WEB_LINKS`, including “never invent a URL” and “link only an address returned by a tool this turn” ([converse.ts:476](/var/tmp/spideryarn-worktrees/qi-qsy8nqyt-guide-reads-pages/src/converse.ts:476)). The guide deliberately omits it because it was written when the guide had no page tool ([converse.ts:1719](/var/tmp/spideryarn-worktrees/qi-qsy8nqyt-guide-reads-pages/src/converse.ts:1719)); its current linking instruction is specific to `search_web` ([converse.ts:1915](/var/tmp/spideryarn-worktrees/qi-qsy8nqyt-guide-reads-pages/src/converse.ts:1915)). Without a Markdown link in the answer, `WebSources` has nothing to render even though the tool row says “read example.com” ([ChatPanel.tsx:2985](/var/tmp/spideryarn-worktrees/qi-qsy8nqyt-guide-reads-pages/src/web/ChatPanel.tsx:2985)).  
+Recommended change: interpolate `WEB_LINKS`, or a deliberately equivalent guide-specific shared rule, into `GUIDE_SYSTEM`; test that the prompt carries the no-invented-URL rule. No other client change is needed: tool rows already support `read_web_page`, and Bring-into-chat remains Chat-only because `bring` is created only for `kind === "chat"` ([ChatPanel.tsx:1647](/var/tmp/spideryarn-worktrees/qi-qsy8nqyt-guide-reads-pages/src/web/ChatPanel.tsx:1647)).
+
+F3 — P1 — The eval cannot currently support its cost and handoff claims.  
+Evidence: the plan says it will measure reads, searches, seconds, words, and whether `since` still hands off to Chat ([plan:202](/var/tmp/spideryarn-worktrees/qi-qsy8nqyt-guide-reads-pages/docs/plans/261017e-bring-a-web-page-into-chat.md:202)). The eval discards complete `ToolRun` records into name strings ([chat-web-reach.ts:330](/var/tmp/spideryarn-worktrees/qi-qsy8nqyt-guide-reads-pages/evals/chat-web-reach.ts:330)), so it cannot see whether `offer_next_steps` actually contained a `chat` step, which address was read, or the read’s elapsed time. Its result shape has no token or dollar cost ([chat-web-reach.ts:254](/var/tmp/spideryarn-worktrees/qi-qsy8nqyt-guide-reads-pages/evals/chat-web-reach.ts:254)), despite `ConverseEvent.done` already exposing turn token usage ([converse.ts:2314](/var/tmp/spideryarn-worktrees/qi-qsy8nqyt-guide-reads-pages/src/converse.ts:2314)). `withLedger` prints only one aggregate total for the whole run. The tools-off guide eval cannot observe page-reading at all ([guide/run.ts:15](/var/tmp/spideryarn-worktrees/qi-qsy8nqyt-guide-reads-pages/evals/guide/run.ts:15)).  
+Recommended change: retain full tool runs; record read count and milliseconds, whether the supplied address was the one requested, whether `since` produced a `chat` step, and `done.usage`. Wrap each case in `collectSpend`, as `evals/guide/run.ts` does, to record dollars and call counts including the search subagent. Run repeated before/after samples. Note explicitly that content quality still requires reading the saved answers.
+
+F4 — P1 — The test and contract-update inventory is incomplete.  
+Evidence: `tests/guide-kind.test.ts` hard-codes the exact guide tool array and will fail when the new tool is inserted ([guide-kind.test.ts:257](/var/tmp/spideryarn-worktrees/qi-qsy8nqyt-guide-reads-pages/tests/guide-kind.test.ts:257)), but the plan names only the gate and web-reach tests. Security-relevant code comments will also become false: `GUIDE_TOOLS` is described as excluding `read_web_page` ([chat-tools.ts:612](/var/tmp/spideryarn-worktrees/qi-qsy8nqyt-guide-reads-pages/src/chat-tools.ts:612)), and `runTool` says a guide asking for it runs nothing ([chat-tools.ts:2544](/var/tmp/spideryarn-worktrees/qi-qsy8nqyt-guide-reads-pages/src/chat-tools.ts:2544)).  
+Recommended change: add `tests/guide-kind.test.ts` and `tests/chat-live-ticket-route.test.ts` to the plan, plus updating these comments and the `GUIDE_SYSTEM` header. Also pin that even a failed/refused first guide read consumes the one-read allowance, matching `search_web`’s before-dispatch accounting.
+
+F5 — P1 — The plan currently claims Stage 2 is built when it is not.  
+Evidence: the status says “built 2026-10-18” ([plan:3](/var/tmp/spideryarn-worktrees/qi-qsy8nqyt-guide-reads-pages/docs/plans/261017e-bring-a-web-page-into-chat.md:3)), while its own “What landed” section says Stage 2 is not built ([plan:285](/var/tmp/spideryarn-worktrees/qi-qsy8nqyt-guide-reads-pages/docs/plans/261017e-bring-a-web-page-into-chat.md:285)); the implementation files are unchanged. The eval also speaks in present tense as though the guide already has the tool ([chat-web-reach.ts:192](/var/tmp/spideryarn-worktrees/qi-qsy8nqyt-guide-reads-pages/evals/chat-web-reach.ts:192)).  
+Recommended change: mark 2B approved/planned until it lands, then update Status, What landed, eval comments, the question’s status, and project docs together with the implementation commit.
+
+F6 — P2 — The final-round nudge still describes only article tools.  
+Evidence: after the tool-round cap, guide turns are told that their “article tools” are finished ([converse.ts:3251](/var/tmp/spideryarn-worktrees/qi-qsy8nqyt-guide-reads-pages/src/converse.ts:3251)). That was already incomplete for `search_web` and becomes more misleading with page-reading. `ENDS_THE_TURN` itself remains correct: a page read does not settle, so its result is sent back before ending.  
+Recommended change: say “article and web tools” or simply “looking-up tools”.
+
+F7 — P2 — Two risk statements need narrower wording.  
+Evidence: “Chat stays uncapped” ([plan:161](/var/tmp/spideryarn-worktrees/qi-qsy8nqyt-guide-reads-pages/docs/plans/261017e-bring-a-web-page-into-chat.md:161)) is true only as “Chat has no read-specific counter”: the whole turn still has a 120-second deadline and three tool rounds, although each batch can contain multiple calls ([converse.ts:245](/var/tmp/spideryarn-worktrees/qi-qsy8nqyt-guide-reads-pages/src/converse.ts:245)). Likewise, “three outbound actions” ([plan:181](/var/tmp/spideryarn-worktrees/qi-qsy8nqyt-guide-reads-pages/docs/plans/261017e-bring-a-web-page-into-chat.md:181)) means three model-issued tool calls; one `search_web` call may cause multiple provider searches ([web-search-subagent.ts:4](/var/tmp/spideryarn-worktrees/qi-qsy8nqyt-guide-reads-pages/src/web-search-subagent.ts:4)), and a page fetch may follow redirects. The URL, 12,000-character, and 20-second caps are otherwise stated correctly. The profile claim is accurate for normal turns when those fields exist; absent or unreadable fields are omitted.  
+Recommended change: say “one page-read call plus two search-tool calls” and “Chat keeps its existing lack of a read-specific cap.”
+
+The WeakMap design is sound for typed turns: `converse` creates one context per invocation ([converse.ts:3000](/var/tmp/spideryarn-worktrees/qi-qsy8nqyt-guide-reads-pages/src/converse.ts:3000)) and reuses it for every tool call ([converse.ts:3798](/var/tmp/spideryarn-worktrees/qi-qsy8nqyt-guide-reads-pages/src/converse.ts:3798)); the next turn invokes `converse` again and gets a new context. The only exception that matters is Live, covered by F1.
+
+VERDICT: build with the P1 fixes
